t issue, or set the `overflow` property of `dropdown-menu` to `auto` and limit the height of it by set its `top` property to a fixed value, like `-300px`.\r\n\r\n#### Steps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. Open a flow detail that is short enough\r\n2. Open the view options menu\r\n3. The menu get displayed as shown in the screenshot above\r\n\r\n#### System Information\r\nMitmproxy: 6.0.2\r\nPython: 3.9.1\r\nOpenSSL: OpenSSL 1.1.1i  8 Dec 2020\r\nPlatform: Windows-10-10.0.16299-SP0\r\nFirefox: 86.0b9","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4448/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/4448/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]